# literature.kb — what writing does, and by what means.
#
# `arts.kb` covers the arts broadly and `language.kb` the linguistic machinery. This covers the
# forms, the devices, and — the part a fact store usually loses — what each device is *for*.

literature | is_a=written work valued as art | purpose=representing experience in language | has_kind=prose
poetry | purpose=compressing meaning through sound and form | has_part=metre | has_part=imagery
prose | is_a=literature | means=writing in ordinary sentences rather than verse | has_kind=novel | has_kind=short story | has_kind=essay
drama | purpose=being performed rather than read | has_part=stage direction
novel | is_a=prose | means=an extended fictional narrative | has_part=point of view
short story | is_a=prose | purpose=achieving a single effect in one sitting
essay | is_a=prose | purpose=working out a thought in public
epic | is_a=poetry | means=a long narrative poem about heroic deeds
sonnet | is_a=poetry | means=a poem of fourteen lines | has_property=a turn of thought near the end
haiku | is_a=poetry | means=a very short poem in three lines | purpose=fixing one moment
tragedy | purpose=showing a person destroyed by a flaw or a fate | has_part=hamartia | causes=catharsis in the audience
comedy | purpose=ending in reconciliation rather than in loss
satire | is_a=form | purpose=attacking a folly by exaggerating it | requires=a shared target the reader recognises
allegory | is_a=form | means=a story whose surface stands for something else throughout
fable | is_a=short story with a moral | purpose=teaching by an example that is not human
myth | is_a=traditional story | purpose=explaining an origin or a practice within a culture

# --- the machinery ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ #
plot | is_a=the arrangement of events in a narrative | purpose=making one event follow from another rather than merely after it | has_part=exposition | has_part=rising action | has_part=climax | has_part=resolution
conflict | is_a=opposition that drives a narrative | purpose=giving the events a direction | has_kind=internal conflict | has_kind=external conflict
character | is_a=a person in a narrative | has_kind=protagonist | has_kind=antagonist | has_kind=foil
protagonist | means=the one whose choices the story follows
foil | is_a=character | purpose=showing another character more clearly by contrast
point of view | is_a=the position from which a story is told | purpose=deciding what the reader can know | has_kind=first person | has_kind=third person limited | has_kind=omniscient
unreliable narrator | is_a=point of view | means=a narrator the reader has reason to doubt | causes=the reader reading against the telling
setting | is_a=where and when a narrative takes place | purpose=constraining what can happen
theme | is_a=the idea a work keeps returning to | means=what the work is about beneath what happens in it
tone | is_a=the attitude a work takes to its subject
motif | is_a=a recurring image or idea | purpose=binding a work together by repetition
symbol | is_a=a thing that stands for an idea | purpose=carrying meaning that is not stated
imagery | is_a=language that appeals to the senses | purpose=making a scene present rather than described
metaphor | purpose=carrying the structure of one idea onto another
simile | means=a comparison made with like or as
personification | is_a=figure of speech | means=giving human qualities to something that is not human
irony | means=saying one thing while the situation says another | has_kind=verbal irony | has_kind=dramatic irony | has_kind=situational irony
dramatic irony | is_a=irony | occurs_when=the audience knows what a character does not | causes=tension
foreshadowing | is_a=technique | purpose=preparing the reader for what is to come | causes=an ending feeling earned rather than arbitrary
flashback | is_a=technique | purpose=giving the reader a past event where it now matters
in medias res | is_a=technique | means=beginning in the middle of the action | purpose=engaging the reader before explaining
stream of consciousness | is_a=technique | purpose=rendering thought as it runs rather than as it is reported
metre | is_a=the regular rhythm of a line of verse | purpose=giving a poem a pulse | has_kind=iambic pentameter
iambic pentameter | is_a=metre | means=five pairs of an unstressed then a stressed syllable
rhyme | is_a=matching sounds at the ends of lines | purpose=binding lines together and aiding memory
alliteration | is_a=repetition of an initial consonant sound | purpose=drawing lines together by sound
free verse | is_a=poetry without regular metre or rhyme | purpose=letting the form follow the sense
enjambment | is_a=running a sentence past the end of a line | causes=a pull across the line break
catharsis | is_a=effect on an audience | means=the release of pity and fear | occurs_when=a tragedy reaches its end
canon | is_a=the set of works a culture treats as central | causes=some works being taught and others forgotten
literary criticism | is_a=activity | purpose=arguing about what a work means and how it works | requires=close reading
close reading | is_a=method | purpose=basing a claim about a work on its exact words | requires=the text itself
genre | is_a=a category of work with shared conventions | purpose=setting the reader's expectations | causes=a work being read against what its kind usually does
